00:45:02.700 --> 00:45:05.430
the idea of Israel as a Jewish state.

00:45:05.430 --> 00:45:07.790
So the Israel question is really in this,

00:45:07.790 --> 00:45:10.944
in some complicated ways
and has been, you know,

00:45:10.944 --> 00:45:14.860
for Black people in the United
States as a kind of negative,

00:45:14.860 --> 00:45:16.023
you know, sort of check
against them, right?

00:45:16.023 --> 00:45:18.530
Because there's this sense
that develops in the late '60s,

00:45:18.530 --> 00:45:21.950
early '70s, that Black
people are anti-Israel right?

00:45:21.950 --> 00:45:25.750
And in our own moment, the
proponents of the most dangerous

00:45:25.750 --> 00:45:27.870
antisemitism in the
United States, bar none,

00:45:27.870 --> 00:45:29.350
are people who support Israel.

00:45:29.350 --> 00:45:31.874
And so, we're in this very complicated

00:45:31.874 --> 00:45:35.293
sort of religious,
racial, political moment.

00:45:36.800 --> 00:45:37.633
- Great.

00:45:37.633 --> 00:45:40.993
So a question about, you
